{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-4161-r4517293","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Sunglow Motel-Cafe Pickle Pie","sourcePageId":4161,"sourceRevision":"4517293","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-20T22:45:44Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Sunglow%20Motel-Cafe%20Pickle%20Pie&oldid=4517293","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:52.726Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for pies and tarts","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using cucumber pickles","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using light cream","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using nutmeg","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e8c20e095728aa94a21788db74e35d5e2c4ed017d67e422fa38d8c54ed8d75bb","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pie and tart recipes\n| Yield = 2 pies\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Desserts]]\n\nThe Sunglow Motel-Cafe in Bicknell, Utah serves the unique '''pickle pie''', developed by Cula Ekker. This is their recipe, as it appeared in a ''Salt Lake Tribune'' article that is framed and hangs on the cafe's wall.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*5 [[Cookbook:Eggs|eggs]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Lemon extract|lemon extract]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n*1 cup + 2 tbsp light [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]]\n*⅛ cup [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]], melted\n*12 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] sweet [[Cookbook:Pickle|pickles]], drained and ground\n*2 unbaked 9-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|pie shells]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#[[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] eggs and sugar until lemon-colored and thick; beat in cinnamon, nutmeg, lemon extract, cornstarch, cream and margarine. \n#Stir ground sweet pickles into mixture.\n#Pour pickle mixture into unbaked pie shells.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] at 350°F for 1–1.25 hours, until a knife inserted in center comes out clean.\n\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber pickles]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pies and tarts]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using light cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nutmeg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Sunglow Motel-Cafe Pickle Pie","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"5 eggs","sourceText":"5 eggs","amountText":"5 eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cups white granulated sugar","sourceText":"2 cups white granulated sugar","amountText":"2 cups white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tsp cin